WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.499 --> 00:00:04.360
She's Gotta Have It--I was
the Caterer, the Producer,

00:00:04.360 --> 00:00:06.440
the Director, the
Screenwriter, acted in it,

00:00:06.440 --> 00:00:08.440
and I was the 1st--we
didn't have a 1st AD.

00:00:10.891 --> 00:00:11.390
Why?

00:00:11.390 --> 00:00:14.090
We didn't have the money.

00:00:14.090 --> 00:00:16.610
When you're an independent
filmmaker and making films

00:00:16.610 --> 00:00:19.580
outside of Hollywood,
that's hard.

00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:24.800
You have to pray on bended
knee at that church of cinema.

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:28.217
But you have these tools that
could help you tell a story.

00:00:28.217 --> 00:00:29.800
Want to show someone
who is a little weak?

00:00:29.800 --> 00:00:30.770
You shoot them from above.

00:00:30.770 --> 00:00:32.400
Want to show
someone who is powerful?

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:33.910
You shoot them from below.

00:00:33.910 --> 00:00:36.100
Well, there's a
dynamic that you get

00:00:36.100 --> 00:00:38.610
with the movement of camera.

00:00:38.610 --> 00:00:39.750
Film is about movement.

00:00:43.350 --> 00:00:44.089
For the writers--

00:00:44.089 --> 00:00:45.630
You know what
the f*** that means?

00:00:45.630 --> 00:00:48.450
Yeah, it means pay me
my mother******’ money.

00:00:48.450 --> 00:00:49.890
Here's the thing--
why this works.

00:00:49.890 --> 00:00:51.723
When you think about
it, they're both right.

00:00:51.723 --> 00:00:54.540
That really makes s*** dramatic
when both people have beliefs,

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:56.600
and then, you have
them come head to head.

00:00:56.600 --> 00:00:57.670
I owe you fifty bucks.

00:00:57.670 --> 00:00:58.170
You keep it.

00:00:58.170 --> 00:00:58.884
You keep it.

00:00:58.884 --> 00:00:59.550
No, you keep it.

00:00:59.550 --> 00:01:00.390
You keep it.

00:01:06.160 --> 00:01:09.460
There's been a history
of American cinema, which

00:01:09.460 --> 00:01:13.144
has denigrated, defamed,
belittled, dehumanized.

00:01:13.144 --> 00:01:13.810
It's documented.

00:01:13.810 --> 00:01:18.590
The Klan used Birth of a
Nation to lynch black folks.

00:01:18.590 --> 00:01:21.590
As a filmmaker, you know, it's
not something to play with.

00:01:21.590 --> 00:01:27.500
It's going to take many decades
to retell these stories.

00:01:27.500 --> 00:01:31.760
And I knew that one way that I
could do something about this

00:01:31.760 --> 00:01:35.040
was to make films for
a diverse audience

00:01:35.040 --> 00:01:41.030
to show black people in all
our glory, faults, warts,

00:01:41.030 --> 00:01:43.460
and what not.

00:01:43.460 --> 00:01:45.410
Just grab the camera and go.

00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:48.200
Fight to get your
vision on the screen.

00:01:48.200 --> 00:01:51.790
In short of killing
somebody, robbing, I mean,

00:01:51.790 --> 00:01:54.684
you're gonna do what you have
to do to get this thing made.

00:01:54.684 --> 00:01:56.850
Majority of the people on
this earth go to the grave

00:01:56.850 --> 00:02:00.680
having worked a job
they’ve hated their whole life.

00:02:00.680 --> 00:02:05.000
So, if you're able to make a
living doing what you love,

00:02:05.000 --> 00:02:07.190
you've won.

00:02:07.190 --> 00:02:10.420
I'm Spike Lee, and this
is my MasterClass.

